  "notes": "Government heritage records place the Lee Theatre on this site as a major dual opera and cinematic venue. Written architecture and period newspaper reporting describe the marble-faced Beaux-Arts street exterior, flanking columns and small domed entry tower, and a broad dome at the auditorium."
